laceStatsAggExpressionWithEval`.","Once the count normalization happens, the deduplication should kick in (since all counts will be the same) and this type of query should work.\r\nThe critical bit here is normalization so count(*), count(1), count(), count(*) and count(1+1+2) all fold back to the same expression of count(1)."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","id":37859,"created_at":"2024-04-17T10:39:47Z","original_position":21,"side":"LEFT","position":21,"original_start_line":379,"submitted_on_commit":"7706d5f844f1ee0ddc4e694b36df1e052bab09ee","diff_hunk":"@@ -370,42 +370,17 @@ public void testAnotherCountAllWithFilter() {\n         assertThat(expected.toString(), is(esStatsQuery.query().toString()));\n     }\n \n-    /**\n-     * Expected\n-     * ProjectExec[[c{r}#3, c{r}#3 AS call, c_literal{r}#7]]\n-     * \\_LimitExec[1000[INTEGER]]\n-     *   \\_AggregateExec[[],[COUNT([2a][KEYWORD]) AS c, COUNT(1[INTEGER]) AS c_literal],FINAL,null]\n-     *     \\_ExchangeExec[[count{r}#18, seen{r}#19, count{r}#20, seen{r}#21],true]\n-     *       \\_EsStatsQueryExec[test], stats[Stat[name\u003d*, type\u003dCOUNT, query\u003dnull], Stat[name\u003d*, type\u003dCOUNT, query\u003dnull]]],\n-     *         query[{\"esql_single_value\":{\"field\":\"emp_no\",\"next\":{\"range\":{\"emp_no\":{\"gt\":10010,\"boost\":1.0}}},\n-     *         \"source\":\"emp_no \u003e 10010@2:9\"}}][count{r}#23, seen{r}#24, count{r}#25, seen{r}#26], limit[],","submitted_start_line":379,"submitted_line":381},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":17,"uncoveredMatchable":21,"timing":153308,"tokensIn":25875,"tokensOut":1697}